  "text": "318305\nPage 91 of\n103/1119026005\n550.001930.00\n982 RESOLUTN\nClear Creek\nNAWСНАУNААТЬANAR\nClear Creek County's Re-vegetation requirement is: 1) Slopes\nconstructed at >3:1 (horizontal to vertical) can be hand seeded\nand mulched. 2) Slopes constructed at 3:1 to 2:1 to must be\nhydroseeded/hydromulched. 3) Slopes constructed at 2:1 to 1½:1\nmust be hydroseeded/hydromulched and have slope\nnetting/erosion control blankets installed lor equivalent erosion\ncontrol measure with the approval of the Site Development\nInspector). Slopes steeper than 12:1 are not permitted or\nrequire retaining walls.\nPermanent soil stabilization measures shall be installed within\nthirty days after final grade is reached. If construction is\ncompleted during winter months, planting should occur within\nthe next window of opportunity. Silt fence or brush barrier to be\ninstalled on downhill side of excavation.\nDetermining Steepness of Grade\n1.0 ft.\n1.51 (67%)\n.1.0ft.\n23:1 (50%)\n1.5ft.\n2.0 ft.\nMore Difficult To Revegetate\n1.0ft.\n3:1 (33%)\n3.0ft.\nLess Difficult To Revegetate\n91",
